## Graphic / layout audit checklist

Before shipping UI changes, verify in code (templates + CSS), not via browser:

1. **Hierarchy:** one H1; brand/eyebrow not fighting display titles.
2. **Alignment:** title rows use flex with `min-width: 0`, wrap gap, no absolute stacking on text.
3. **Header clearance:** sticky header + `scroll-margin`; strip/hero padding clears nav.
4. **Plan chrome:** `dash-plan--free|plus|business` atmospheres stay distinct without breaking type contrast.
5. **Motion:** 2–3 intentional motions max on marketing; honor `prefers-reduced-motion`.
6. **Density:** one job per section; no card soup in heroes.

---

## Delivery

- Fix graphic issues with focused CSS/template/asset diffs.
- Keep Flask CSS tokens (`--brand-*`) as the single source of the accent color; the React geo-ui bundle (`components/`, `static/geo-ui/`) has its own Tailwind tokens and is not auto-synced — update it separately if asked to touch charts there.
- Update `BRAND.md` only when assets or tokens actually change.
